    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0690" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg605"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/474: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-20T16:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1919,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 21,
                            11.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3033. Department’s telegram 1963 April 11, 7 p.m.<anchor n="89" xml:id="d573-f1"
                    /> Foreign Office states in reply that as all laws mentioned are of a general
                    character all companies and persons are equally bound by them and that the
                    Mexican Government cannot make any exceptions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
